{
  "format": "modbus-read-responses/1",
  "description": "What a collector makes of the bytes it receives after sending a read. Frames are built independently of either collector (CRC-16/MODBUS, check value 0x4B37); each outcome follows the documented rules. expected: the request the reply must answer (transaction_id is 0 and unused for rtu_over_tcp). skipped: every step that drops bytes ahead of the reply, in order: stale (TCP: a whole frame with another transaction id), noise (RTU: a byte that cannot start the reply), bad_crc (RTU: one byte of what began like the reply but failed its CRC). result: the registers read, a Modbus exception code, incomplete (more bytes needed), or an error: malformed_frame, unexpected_response (TCP: the right transaction from another unit), or malformed_response (a frame that is not the reply to this read). rest: the bytes after the reply, or, for incomplete, malformed_frame or unexpected_response, what the buffer still holds when stepping stops. Every implementation that reads meters must give every outcome.",
